Third-party material in this distribution

fabench/dataprep/noisemix/kaldi/ holds data augmentation scripts from the
Kaldi speech recognition toolkit (https://github.com/kaldi-asr/kaldi), under
the Apache License 2.0. Kaldi's COPYING file is kept beside them, and
PROVENANCE.md there records the one local patch.

The TIMIT 61 to 39 phone folding in fabench/normalize/en/maps.py follows
Lee and Hon (1989) and Kaldi's egs/timit/s5/conf/phones.60-48-39.map.

datasets/languages/en/timit/split/dev.list is Kaldi's
egs/timit/s5/conf/dev_spk.list. datasets/languages/en/timit/split/core_test.list
and datasets/languages/en/buckeye/speakers.tsv restate speaker and utterance
facts from the TIMIT and Buckeye corpus documentation. They carry no corpus
audio and no corpus text.

The noise conditions are built from MUSAN (OpenSLR 17, CC BY 4.0) and the
simulated room impulse responses of RIRS_NOISES (OpenSLR 28, Apache 2.0).
Neither is distributed with this software.
